Write a batch runner over a mutants.json file (subject, spec, old, new, label) that wraps the existing mutate.sh exit codes (0 RED / 1 SURVIVED / 3 COULD NOT CHECK). It:
- runs the identity mutant first;
- prints the RED/SURVIVED/COULD-NOT-CHECK denominator;
- emits `Mutation-Proof:` trailer lines ready to paste;
- refuses to run outside a linked worktree.

Rewrite the hand-written sections to target_shape item 1. Leave all three generated marker pairs untouched.
- Layout: ROOT = `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, APP = ROOT/frontend. The tree names STATUS.md, .claude/rules/, ci/pipeline.sh and .githooks/, and drops the 4 HISTORICAL memory/ filenames and the S0-S4 status. 'Restate ROOT/APP in every Explore or Plan brief.'
- Stack: 4 bullets. (1) Monolithic by design; Components.jsx is the irreducible Player loop and the other ≥900-LOC files carry no such finding. (2) ECS is a narrow slice; keep the grep command, drop the count. (3) The engine-core keep list. (4) Touch is built; real-device feel is Kevin-gated.
- Hard rules, each naming its enforcer:
  - game-loop isolation;
  - no in-place rewrites of src JS(X) (B2);
  - the design-language lock, dropping the 'said 7' clause;
  - capture guards RESET, never early-return (the capture-guard-timing gate);
  - done means proven to RUN (e2e, a probe or a log line you watched fire), plus 'what passes if the feature is deleted';
  - one plan doc per milestone;
  - commits: no attribution (pre-commit guard and opsec-scan); fix-ups are new commits (B1 deny); Mutation-Proof:/Baseline-Review: trailers;
  - a violated rule gets a checkpoint or a deterministic layer, not more prose;
  - the global ACTIVE_PLAN rule replaces the local tunneling thresholds.
- Gates: add a test:look row and 3 visual one-liners: (1) port 4178 with --strictPort, so never run two captures; (2) capture mode suppresses weather, mobs, NPCs and particles, so judge looks from non-capture frames; (3) read provenance.ua and re-measure, never quote.
- Process hygiene, 3 bullets: _serve.mjs plus the SessionEnd sweep; close-surface is denied; check uptime and R-state before blaming a gate.
- Models, 2 lines: Crafty reviewers and verifiers run at xhigh, never max (DECISIONS 2026-10-27); `/code-review xhigh` is the default review; Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5 run mechanical lanes with the full model id and an explicit effort.
- Compaction & resume, about 0.7 KB: preserve the milestone and plan path, the resume pointer, uncommitted files, standing directives and /loop state; preserve gate COMMANDS, never results.
- /loop: one line.
Delete: the size-history paragraph, the de-monolith history, the browser incident narrative, the VOID determinism narrative, the denominator paragraph, Read-Before-Write, Initialization, the Session-Documentation list and the preambles. Also delete the Core Agent Skills section: its open cleanup/accretion question becomes one ▢ STATUS row, and the Dependabot half goes because .github/dependabot.yml exists.
Record the pre-trim SHA in a DECISIONS entry ('restore any section with git show <sha>:.agent/AGENTS.md'); any narrative not already held by DECISIONS, the rules or a script docblock goes into that entry. Re-point the charter's L60 Method citation and its L316-318 hygiene pointer, and the kernel's L151 pointer, to the new headings and gates-and-probes.md. Lower the .agent/AGENTS.md opsec ledger entry from 3 to 0.

1. Cut the rule to a checklist of about 80 lines:
   - print and assert the denominator;
   - assert presence before absence;
   - mutation-prove, and restore from cp, never checkout;
   - reference values must vary on every weighted axis;
   - make the subject drivable rather than tightening a regex;
   - check both sides of a producer/consumer seam;
   - a swallowed wait means grep the flag's other consumers;
   - prove the entry point is REACHED;
   - the siting rule (tests/gates vs tests/scripts and their ratchets);
   - allocate ports via _serve.mjs probePort;
   - kill what you launch.
2. Move verbatim to GATE-INCIDENTS.md: the 20-row incident table, the DEV/PROD and LCP numbers, and the devtools recipe.
3. Drop every embedded count; its 388-assertion figure is now 574 live (lane-measured).
4. Replace 'no instrument' with: 'as of 2026-10-27, surfaces checked: cmux surfaces via close-preview-tabs.sh; not tried: computer-use (orca computer), claude-in-chrome tabs_context'.

Write the plan doc first. Then build a non-gating script that:
- serves the prod preview via _serve.mjs({preview:true});
- launches with run-scenarios.mjs's Metal GPU flags and capture mode OFF;
- shoots fixed camera poses × setTimeOfDay × weather states;
- writes PNGs and an HTML contact sheet, next to the previous SHA's set, into .superpowers/lookbook/<sha>/ (gitignored);
- prints gpu-cost-probe numbers;
- caps frames and duration, with a finally sweep.
Add one line to AGENTS: 'npm run look:book: real-GPU, capture-off frames to judge looks by eye'.
